  "problem": "What is the minor of ${m}_{31}$ in the matrix\n$M=[\\begin{aligned}-50 & g & f \\\\ f & {g}^{2} & {f}^{2} \\\\ 20g & g & -5\\end{aligned}]?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}\u2217 & g & f \\\\ \u2217 & {g}^{2} & {f}^{2} \\\\ 20g & \u2217 & \u2217\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}g & f \\\\ {g}^{2} & {f}^{2}\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}g & f \\\\ {g}^{2} & {f}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =g\\cdot {f}^{2}-f\\cdot {g}^{2} \\\\  & =g{f}^{2}-f{g}^{2} \\\\  & =gf(f-g)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
